   <media:thumbnail url="https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/brC-o5y0ArY/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>What happens when you turn a sophisticated cruiser into an aggressive grand tourer? Meet the Toyota Crown Signia GT-S Concept, built for the 2026 SEMA Show. Step inside Toyota Motor North America’s Motorsports Garage in Plano, Texas, as the fabrication team builds a one-of-a-kind sports wagon from the ground up—featuring a 4-inch wider stance, custom bodywork, Lexus brakes, bespoke sport seats, and 45-hour 3D-printed components. Watch more SEMA content: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PhwzNdU9S64&amp;list=PLsOvRYzJPCwUOCtl_IzAzuB063QdnmDPS


Explore new Toyota videos: 
▶ https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EbFzyLO124s&amp;list=PLsOvRYzJPCwVPnQZg9qWBpGP8oHLM1aT_
▶ https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zOiZj9No3uU&amp;list=PLsOvRYzJPCwWVhxiSlc1kUCIGX4N6KUNA

Subscribe for more Toyota videos: http://bit.ly/ToyotaSubscribe 

Connect with Toyota USA online:
Visit the Toyota WEBSITE: http://bit.ly/ToyotaSite 
Like Toyota on FACEBOOK: http://bit.ly/ToyotaUSAFB
Follow Toyota on INSTAGRAM: http://bit.ly/ToyotaInsta 

Go behind the scenes with the Toyota Motorsports Garage to see how custom fabrication transforms factory designs into visionary showstoppers. Following in the footsteps of legendary builds like Tacozilla, the FJ Bruiser, and the Time Attack bZ, the Crown Signia GT-S Concept pushes the boundaries of automotive performance, custom body styling, and modern craftsmanship. Learn how our master fabricators blend high-tech 3D printing with precision hand-finishing to create the ultimate grand touring machine. Subscribe to the official Toyota USA YouTube channel for exclusive custom car builds, SEMA reveals, and automotive engineering stories.

#ToyotaUSA #SEMA2026 #CrownSigniaGTS</media:description>
